## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design end-to-end performance plans for multi‑component, GPU-accelerated pipelines and backpressure handling under bursty traffic.

## Key Concepts

- Mixed workload modeling (reads, compute, cache misses)
- Tail latency, backpressure and queueing theory
- GPU batching, warmup, autoscaling on non-uniform metrics
- Observability: GPU, Redis, Kafka metrics; failure modes

## Code Example

```javascript
// k6 pseudo script to model mixed workload
import http from 'k6/http';
import { sleep } from 'k6';
export default function () {
  http.get('https://service/recommend');
  sleep(0.01);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate that autoscaling responds within SLO during a burst?
- Which backends are most susceptible to backpressure and why?

